# LumaLoop mobile — environment template (ADO #129, M5; ADO #131, M7). Copy to
# `.env`, `.env.development`, and `.env.production` (all gitignored per the repo's
# secrets policy) and set per environment. Expo inlines `EXPO_PUBLIC_*` vars at
# build time.
#
# Telemetry ingestion base URL. The RN telemetry client POSTs each event to
# `${EXPO_PUBLIC_API_BASE_URL}/api/event` — the SAME deployed Vercel ingestion as
# the web app (→ Supabase `telemetry_events`). No trailing slash. If unset, the
# client falls back to the documented default in `src/telemetry/endpoint.ts`.
#
# PRODUCTION (ADO #131): the value below is our STABLE Vercel production alias,
# scoped to our project. Use it for `.env.production`. The value is NOT a secret
# (no keys ship in the client).
#
# DO NOT use `https://luma-loop.vercel.app` — that global name belongs to an
# UNRELATED project (a bottle company); it is NOT ours.
#
# NOTE (ADO #82): our production alias is currently behind Vercel Deployment
# Protection (returns HTTP 401 to anonymous clients), so device telemetry POSTs
# will NOT land until the owner turns Deployment Protection OFF (or to "Only
# Preview Deployments"). Until then the client retry-queues gracefully (no crash,
# no data). See mobile/RUN_IOS.md.
EXPO_PUBLIC_API_BASE_URL=https://luma-loop-madhursethji-7775s-projects.vercel.app

# ── Accounts pivot (Supabase Auth + profiles/game_plays) ──────────────────────
# The native app gates the feed behind a Supabase account + profile and records a
# `game_plays` row per resolved card for the signed-in user. It uses the SAME
# Supabase project as the web app. These are PUBLIC client values (not secrets):
# the publishable/anon key ships in the bundle and RLS is the security boundary.
# Expo inlines `EXPO_PUBLIC_*` at build time, so set them before building.
#
# Get them from the Supabase dashboard → Project Settings → API:
#   EXPO_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL       = your project URL
#   EXPO_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY  = the publishable (anon) key
#
# The OAuth/magic-link redirect is the custom scheme deep link
# `lumaloop://auth/callback` (app.json `scheme: "lumaloop"`). It MUST be added to
# the Supabase dashboard → Authentication → URL Configuration → Redirect URLs
# allowlist, or sign-in is rejected. See docs/AUTH_SETUP.md §5.
EXPO_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=https://your-project.supabase.co
EXPO_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=your-publishable-anon-key
